<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chahar Province</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chahar Province was a province of the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, created in 1928 from a special district north-west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a>, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhangjiakou">Kalgan</a> (Zhangjiakou). Named after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chahar-mongols">Chahar Mongols</a>, it combined Mongol grazing lands with Chinese farming districts. Japanese forces occupied it in 1937, and it became part of the Mengjiang client state. The People's Republic dissolved the province in 1952, dividing it between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inner-mongolia">Inner Mongolia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebei">Hebei</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chahar-province.jpg" alt="Chahar Province" width="320" height="250" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lilauid · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Republic_of_China_edcp_location_map_(disputed_territories)_Chahar.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
